          },
          "schemas": {
            "reply": {
              "response": "schema://ToolResponse"
            },
            "output": {
              "arguments": "schema://get_my_loans_Args"
            }
          },
          "name": "get_my_loans_flow"
        },
        {
          "description": "Find Kestrel Bank branches by city (or branch name, state or ZIP). Public information: no verification or session token needed. Pass an empty city to list all branches. Returns address, phone and opening hours, or NOT_FOUND.",
          "settings": {
            "handlerType": "Tool",
            "resourceUri": "",
            "handlerName": "find_branch",
            "handlerDescription": "Find Kestrel Bank branches by city (or branch name, state or ZIP). Public information: no verification or session token needed. Pass an empty city to list all branches. Returns address, phone and opening hours, or NOT_FOUND.",
            "toolTitle": "",
            "readOnlyToolHint": true,
            "destructiveToolHint": false,
            "idempotentToolHint": true,
            "openWorldToolHint": false,
            "scope": ""
          },
          "action": {
            "ref": "github.com/project-flogo/flow",
            "settings": {
              "flowURI": "res://flow:find_branch_flow"
            },
            "input": {
              "arguments": "=$.arguments"
            },
            "output": {
              "response": "=$.response"
            }
          },
          "reply": {
            "outputSchema": ""
          },
          "schemas": {
            "reply": {
              "response": "schema://ToolResponse"
            },
            "output": {
              "arguments": "schema://find_branch_Args"
            }
          },
          "name": "find_branch_flow"
        },
        {
          "description": "Step 1 of 2 for blocking a lost, stolen, damaged or compromised card. Give the card (card_id such as CARD-9001, or its last 4 digits) and the reason: LOST, STOLEN, DAMAGED or SUSPECTED_FRAUD. The system checks every rule and returns PROPOSED with an action_id and the replacement card&#39;s expected delivery date, or NOT_PROPOSED with reason_code CARD_NOT_FOUND (no card of this customer matches), ALREADY_BLOCKED, CARD_EXPIRED, BAD_REASON or SESSION_INVALID. Nothing changes until confirm_card_block is called after the customer&#39;s explicit yes.",
          "settings": {
            "handlerType": "Tool",
            "resourceUri": "",
            "handlerName": "propose_card_block",
            "handlerDescription": "Step 1 of 2 for blocking a lost, stolen, damaged or compromised card. Give the card (card_id such as CARD-9001, or its last 4 digits) and the reason: LOST, STOLEN, DAMAGED or SUSPECTED_FRAUD. The system checks every rule and returns PROPOSED with an action_id and the replacement card's expected delivery date, or NOT_PROPOSED with reason_code CARD_NOT_FOUND (no card of this customer matches), ALREADY_BLOCKED, CARD_EXPIRED, BAD_REASON or SESSION_INVALID. Nothing changes until confirm_card_block is called after the customer's explicit yes.",
            "toolTitle": "",
            "readOnlyToolHint": false,
            "destructiveToolHint": false,
            "idempotentToolHint": true,
            "openWorldToolHint": false,
            "scope": ""
          },
          "action": {
            "ref": "github.com/project-flogo/flow",
            "settings": {
              "flowURI": "res://flow:propose_card_block_flow"
            },
            "input": {
              "arguments": "=$.arguments"
            },
            "output": {
              "response": "=$.response"
            }
          },
          "reply": {
            "outputSchema": ""
          },
          "schemas": {
            "reply": {
              "response": "schema://ToolResponse"
            },
            "output": {
              "arguments": "schema://propose_card_block_Args"
            }
          },
          "name": "propose_card_block_flow"
        },
        {
          "description": "Step 2 of 2: block the card the customer has explicitly confirmed. Pass the action_id from propose_card_block. The system re-checks every rule; proposals expire after 15 minutes. Returns EXECUTED with block_id (BLK-NNNNN) and the replacement&#39;s expected delivery date, or NOT_EXECUTED with reason_code NO_SUCH_PROPOSAL, EXPIRED, ALREADY_EXECUTED, SESSION_INVALID or a rule&#39;s code. Only call after the customer says yes to the exact proposal; never call it without a fresh action_id.",
          "settings": {
            "handlerType": "Tool",
            "resourceUri": "",
            "handlerName": "confirm_card_block",
            "handlerDescription": "Step 2 of 2: block the card the customer has explicitly confirmed. Pass the action_id from propose_card_block. The system re-checks every rule; proposals expire after 15 minutes. Returns EXECUTED with block_id (BLK-NNNNN) and the replacement's expected delivery date, or NOT_EXECUTED with reason_code NO_SUCH_PROPOSAL, EXPIRED, ALREADY_EXECUTED, SESSION_INVALID or a rule's code. Only call after the customer says yes to the exact proposal; never call it without a fresh action_id.",
            "toolTitle": "",
            "readOnlyToolHint": false,
            "destructiveToolHint": false,
            "idempotentToolHint": true,
            "openWorldToolHint": false,
            "scope": ""
          },
          "action": {
            "ref": "github.com/project-flogo/flow",
            "settings": {
              "flowURI": "res://flow:confirm_card_block_flow"
            },
            "input": {
              "arguments": "=$.arguments"
            },
            "output": {
              "response": "=$.response"
            }
          },
          "reply": {
            "outputSchema": ""
          },
          "schemas": {
            "reply": {
              "response": "schema://ToolResponse"
            },
            "output": {
              "arguments": "schema://confirm_card_block_Args"
            }
          },
          "name": "confirm_card_block_flow"
        },
        {
          "description": "Step 1 of 2 for disputing a card or account charge. Give the transaction_id (from get_my_transactions), the reason_code (UNRECOGNISED, FRAUD, DUPLICATE, NOT_RECEIVED, NOT_AS_DESCRIBED, CANCELLED_RECURRING or WRONG_AMOUNT) and the customer&#39;s own words. The system checks eligibility and computes the quote: returns PROPOSED with action_id, amount, merchant, provisional_credit, fraud_review and est_decision_date, or NOT_PROPOSED with reason_code NOT_YOUR_TRANSACTION, NOT_A_DEBIT, PENDING_NOT_POSTED, OUTSIDE_WINDOW (older than 120 days), ALREADY_DISPUTED, BAD_REASON, NOT_DUPLICATE or SESSION_INVALID. Read the amount, provisional credit and decision date back exactly as returned; never compute or promise them yourself. Nothing is filed until confirm_dispute.",
          "settings": {
            "handlerType": "Tool",
            "resourceUri": "",
            "handlerName": "propose_dispute",
            "handlerDescription": "Step 1 of 2 for disputing a card or account charge. Give the transaction_id (from get_my_transactions), the reason_code (UNRECOGNISED, FRAUD, DUPLICATE, NOT_RECEIVED, NOT_AS_DESCRIBED, CANCELLED_RECURRING or WRONG_AMOUNT) and the customer's own words. The system checks eligibility and computes the quote: returns PROPOSED with action_id, amount, merchant, provisional_credit, fraud_review and est_decision_date, or NOT_PROPOSED with reason_code NOT_YOUR_TRANSACTION, NOT_A_DEBIT, PENDING_NOT_POSTED, OUTSIDE_WINDOW (older than 120 days), ALREADY_DISPUTED, BAD_REASON, NOT_DUPLICATE or SESSION_INVALID. Read the amount, provisional credit and decision date back exactly as returned; never compute or promise them yourself. Nothing is filed until confirm_dispute.",
            "toolTitle": "",
            "readOnlyToolHint": false,
            "destructiveToolHint": false,
            "idempotentToolHint": true,
            "openWorldToolHint": false,
            "scope": ""
          },
          "action": {
            "ref": "github.com/project-flogo/flow",
            "settings": {
              "flowURI": "res://flow:propose_dispute_flow"
            },
            "input": {
              "arguments": "=$.arguments"
            },
            "output": {
              "response": "=$.response"
            }
          },
          "reply": {
            "outputSchema": ""
          },
          "schemas": {
            "reply": {
              "response": "schema://ToolResponse"
            },
            "output": {
              "arguments": "schema://propose_dispute_Args"
            }
          },
          "name": "propose_dispute_flow"
        },
        {
          "description": "Step 2 of 2: file the dispute the customer has explicitly confirmed. Pass the action_id from propose_dispute. The system re-checks every rule; proposals expire after 15 minutes. Returns FILED with dispute_id (DSP-2026-NNNN), the provisional credit posted (if any), whether Fraud Operations opened a review case, and the decision date; or NOT_FILED with reason_code NO_SUCH_PROPOSAL, EXPIRED, ALREADY_EXECUTED, SESSION_INVALID or a rule&#39;s code. Only call after the customer says yes to the exact proposal.",
          "settings": {
            "handlerType": "Tool",
            "resourceUri": "",
            "handlerName": "confirm_dispute",
            "handlerDescription": "Step 2 of 2: file the dispute the customer has explicitly confirmed. Pass the action_id from propose_dispute. The system re-checks every rule; proposals expire after 15 minutes. Returns FILED with dispute_id (DSP-2026-NNNN), the provisional credit posted (if any), whether Fraud Operations opened a review case, and the decision date; or NOT_FILED with reason_code NO_SUCH_PROPOSAL, EXPIRED, ALREADY_EXECUTED, SESSION_INVALID or a rule's code. Only call after the customer says yes to the exact proposal.",
            "toolTitle": "",
            "readOnlyToolHint": false,
            "destructiveToolHint": false,
            "idempotentToolHint": true,
            "openWorldToolHint": false,
            "scope": ""
          },
          "action": {
            "ref": "github.com/project-flogo/flow",
            "settings": {
              "flowURI": "res://flow:confirm_dispute_flow"
            },
            "input": {
              "arguments": "=$.arguments"
            },
            "output": {
              "response": "=$.response"
            }
          },
          "reply": {
            "outputSchema": ""
          },
          "schemas": {
            "reply": {
              "response": "schema://ToolResponse"
            },
            "output": {
              "arguments": "schema://confirm_dispute_Args"
            }
          },
          "name": "confirm_dispute_flow"
        },
        {
          "description": "Hand a request that needs a human to the right team: FEE_REFUND (refund of a fee such as overdraft or late fee; reference_id = the fee&#39;s transaction_id), LOAN_HARDSHIP (payment difficulty or deferral; reference_id = the loan_id; brief = the hardship intake brief), CREDIT_LIMIT_INCREASE, COMPLAINT, PERSONAL_DETAILS_CHANGE (address, phone, name), ACCOUNT_CLOSURE, BEREAVEMENT, FRAUD_REVIEW or OTHER. The system routes it, works out what a person could approve (e.g. refund that fee, defer up to 3 loan payments) and returns CASE_OPENED with case_id (CASE-NNNNN), team, reply time and requested amount, ALREADY_OPEN when the same request is already with the team, or NOT_OPENED with BAD_TYPE, BAD_REFERENCE or SESSION_INVALID. A person decides; the assistant never decides, approves, promises or predicts the outcome of these requests.",
          "settings": {
            "handlerType": "Tool",
            "resourceUri": "",
            "handlerName": "open_service_case",
            "handlerDescription": "Hand a request that needs a human to the right team: FEE_REFUND (refund of a fee such as overdraft or late fee; reference_id = the fee's transaction_id), LOAN_HARDSHIP (payment difficulty or deferral; reference_id = the loan_id; brief = the hardship intake brief), CREDIT_LIMIT_INCREASE, COMPLAINT, PERSONAL_DETAILS_CHANGE (address, phone, name), ACCOUNT_CLOSURE, BEREAVEMENT, FRAUD_REVIEW or OTHER. The system routes it, works out what a person could approve (e.g. refund that fee, defer up to 3 loan payments) and returns CASE_OPENED with case_id (CASE-NNNNN), team, reply time and requested amount, ALREADY_OPEN when the same request is already with the team, or NOT_OPENED with BAD_TYPE, BAD_REFERENCE or SESSION_INVALID. A person decides; the assistant never decides, approves, promises or predicts the outcome of these requests.",
            "toolTitle": "",
            "readOnlyToolHint": false,
            "destructiveToolHint": false,
            "idempotentToolHint": true,
            "openWorldToolHint": false,
            "scope": ""
          },
          "action": {
            "ref": "github.com/project-flogo/flow",
            "settings": {
              "flowURI": "res://flow:open_service_case_flow"
            },
            "input": {
              "arguments": "=$.arguments"
            },
            "output": {
              "response": "=$.response"
            }
          },
          "reply": {
            "outputSchema": ""
          },
          "schemas": {
            "reply": {
              "response": "schema://ToolResponse"
            },
            "output": {
              "arguments": "schema://open_service_case_Args"
            }
          },
          "name": "open_service_case_flow"
        },
        {
          "description": "List the verified customer&#39;s disputes (DSP-) and service cases (CASE-) with type, status (OPEN, APPROVED, REJECTED for cases), assigned team, amount, provisional credit, the expected decision or reply date and - once a person has decided - the approved amount and the customer_message from the team. Use it when the customer asks about the status of a request, a payment security check or a hardship case.",
          "settings": {
            "handlerType": "Tool",
            "resourceUri": "",
            "handlerName": "get_my_cases",
            "handlerDescription": "List the verified customer's disputes (DSP-) and service cases (CASE-) with type, status (OPEN, APPROVED, REJECTED for cases), assigned team, amount, provisional credit, the expected decision or reply date and - once a person has decided - the approved amount and the customer_message from the team. Use it when the customer asks about the status of a request, a payment security check or a hardship case.",
            "toolTitle": "",
            "readOnlyToolHint": true,
            "destructiveToolHint": false,
            "idempotentToolHint": true,
            "openWorldToolHint": false,
            "scope": ""
          },
          "action": {
            "ref": "github.com/project-flogo/flow",
